        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W4408_Assoc9_di" bpmnElement="W4408_Assoc9"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5555" name="W5555. Customer or Visitor Death on Premises — Scene Protocol, Family Liaison &amp; Trading-Continuity Decision" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A customer or visitor dies on premises — sudden natural death (cardiac, stroke), fatal accident (fall, struck-by), or unattended death discovered on site — before any police determination of cause
Frequency: The rare fatality tail of the ~daily chain-wide customer-incident population (W4401): a small number of events per year across ~205 sites serving ~99,000 people on premises per day (customers + staff, the W330 population canon)
Volume: 1 event × the site&#x27;s trading surface (partial closure with a screened area, or full closure, for 2–12 hours) × responders (Store Manager, security, first aider, PNP/SOCO) × the notification set (family, insurer per W4405, DOLE only where an employee is involved, comms only if public)
Owner: Store Manager / Head of HSE
Participants: Security Guard, First Aider (VS-83), Regional Manager, Head of Customer Safety, HSE Manager (VS-24), Legal Counsel (VS-100), HR Business Partner (employee-involved cases; W1325 death-in-service benefits), Insurance Coordinator (W4403/W4405), EAP Counselor (W2867), Corporate Communications (W134/W855 if the event becomes public), PNP Scene of the Crime Operations (SOCO) team, Barangay officials
Source: workflow W5555 — Customer or Visitor Death on Premises — Scene Protocol, Family Liaison &amp; Trading-Continuity Decision</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5555_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5555_Lane1" name="First Aider">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5555_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5555_Lane3" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5555_Lane4" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5555_Lane5" name="Head of Customer Safety">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5555_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5555_Start7" name="A customer or visitor dies on premises — sudden natural death (cardiac, stroke), fatal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task8" name="Response until pronouncement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Response until pronouncement: first aid and resuscitation attempts continue per the First Aider protocol until medical personnel formally pronounce — abandonment before pronouncement is both a welfare and a legal failure; emergency services called immediately
Responsible (R): First Aider / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task9" name="Scene control — nothing moves">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scene control — nothing moves: screen or cordon the area; halt all cleaning; hold CCTV footage (W838 preservation request); the decedent&#x27;s belongings are not touched or photographed by staff; access limited to responders
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task10" name="Police handoff &amp; scene release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Police handoff &amp; scene release: PNP/SOCO take custody and conduct their on-site processing; the scene is released to BuildRight only on their documented clearance; Barangay assists family tracing where identity or next-of-kin is unresolved
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Security Guard
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task11" name="Family care &amp; liaison">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Family care &amp; liaison: a private space away from the scene; factual briefing only with the W4401 no-admission-of-liability rule; written contact log; religious/cultural needs accommodated; family never learns of the death from social media (Step 3/4 sequencing rule)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: Same day + aftercare</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task12" name="Trading-continuity decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Trading-continuity decision: Regional Manager with the Head of Customer Safety decides and documents — full closure, partial closure with a screened area, or continued trading; where the scene is visible to customers, the dignity-first default is closure until screened; the decision and its basis are recorded either way
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Within 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task13" name="Employee care">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Employee care: witnessing staff stood down for the shift where feasible; critical-incident stress debriefing per W2867; no same-day formal statements (memory-contamination rule)
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / EAP Counselor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task14" name="Documentation &amp; statutory notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Documentation &amp; statutory notification: incident file per W4402 with restricted visibility; insurer notification per W4405 within 24 hours; employee-involved deaths add the DOLE 24-hour report and the W1325 benefits chain; privacy handling of the decedent&#x27;s data per VS-91
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Customer Safety
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: Within 24–48 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5555_Task15" name="Aftercare &amp; CAPA">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Aftercare &amp; CAPA: structured family follow-up; claim handling per W4403 under an empathy protocol (claim defense never argued at the scene); hazard-CAPA per W4404 where the death followed an accident; protocol learnings folded into the W4406 drill rotation
Responsible (R): Head of Customer Safety / Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Safety
Duration: 2–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5555_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5555_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5555_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5555_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-673 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Incident Response, Claims &amp; Safety Analytics (PA-147.3).) | - operational: scene released only on documented PNP/SOCO clearance filed in the incident record; trading-continuity decision documented with its basis before either closing or continuing; decedent and family data handled per the restricted-visibility privacy rule
Owner: Store Manager / Head of HSE</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5555_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5555_Annotation17" targetRef="W5555_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow19" sourceRef="W5555_Start7" targetRef="W5555_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow20" sourceRef="W5555_Task8" targetRef="W5555_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow21" sourceRef="W5555_Task9" targetRef="W5555_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow22" sourceRef="W5555_Task10" targetRef="W5555_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow23" sourceRef="W5555_Task11" targetRef="W5555_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow24" sourceRef="W5555_Task12" targetRef="W5555_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow25" sourceRef="W5555_Task13" targetRef="W5555_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow26" sourceRef="W5555_Task14" targetRef="W5555_Task15" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5555_Flow27" sourceRef="W5555_Task15" targetRef="W5555_End16" />
    </bpmn:process>
